The following parts are adapted from Auto Ontology source files:
- Modeling, relationship, SQL attribute, entity extraction, SQL writing and
  answer validation rules (src/auto_ontology_mcp/guidance.py), from
  auto_ontology/semantic/term_extractor.py, semantic/fk_suggester.py,
  semantic/semantic_fk.py, semantic/sql_attribute_suggester.py,
  retrieval/entity_coverage/prompts.py, retrieval/text_to_sql/prompts.py and
  skills/nvidia-ontology-query/references/query-validation.md.
- Column profiling and date format inference (src/auto_ontology_mcp/profiling.py),
  from semantic/visit_enter.py and semantic/date_format.py.
- Expression mining for SQL attribute suggestions
  (src/auto_ontology_mcp/sqlcheck.py: extract_expressions), from
  semantic/sql_attribute_suggester.py.
- Literal and join probes (src/auto_ontology_mcp/validation.py), following
  retrieval/text_to_sql/db_probe/literal_check.py and join_path_check.py.
- Checks on the parsed query (src/auto_ontology_mcp/structure.py): integer division, from
  retrieval/text_to_sql/db_probe/literal_check.py; placeholder queries, a GROUP BY on a
  primary key, a many-side column selected next to an aggregate and unquoted mixed-case
  identifiers, from retrieval/text_to_sql/agents/sql_parse_validation.py.

Changes: the LLM, embedding and reranking calls were removed. The MCP client's
model performs those steps through the tools, and the server keeps the
deterministic parts (catalog extraction, profiling, key inference, validation
and read-only execution) on a local SQLite store instead of Postgres/pgvector.

